  "question": {
    "text": "If $f: R \\rightarrow R$ satisfies $f(x+y)=f(x)+f(y)$, for all $x, y \\in R$ and $f(1)=7$, then $\\sum_{r=1}^n f(r)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "5saRS",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{7 n(n+1)}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ZpDaf",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{7 \\mathrm{n}}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NLahy",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{7(\\mathrm{n}+1)}{2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "fUqVl",
      "text": "\n$7 n+(n+1)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x}+\\mathrm{y})=\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})+\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{y}) . \\quad$ Let $\\mathrm{f}(\\alpha)=\\mathrm{m} \\alpha$\n$\\mathrm{f}(1)=7 ; \\quad \\therefore \\mathrm{m}=7, \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=7 \\mathrm{x}$\n$\\sum_{\\mathrm{r}=1}^{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{r})=7 \\sum_1^{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{r}=\\frac{7 \\mathrm{n}(\\mathrm{n}+1)}{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
